Subject: [PATCH] kbase: guard __clk_is_enabled behind CONFIG_COMMON_CLK

Build fix, not a behaviour change.

r54p0 calls __clk_is_enabled() unconditionally in two places in
mali_kbase_core_linux.c, and includes <linux/clk-provider.h> without a
guard. The declaration of __clk_is_enabled() in include/linux/clk-provider.h
is NOT inside an #ifdef CONFIG_COMMON_CLK, so this code compiles cleanly on
any kernel. The definition, however, lives in drivers/clk/clk.c, which is
built only as obj-$(CONFIG_COMMON_CLK). Every other clk_* function used at
these two sites (clk_disable, clk_put, clk_unprepare, clk_prepare) is a
no-op static inline stub when CONFIG_COMMON_CLK is unset; __clk_is_enabled
is the one exception, and it has no stub.

Consequence: when CONFIG_COMMON_CLK is unset the module compiles but fails
to link:

    ERROR: modpost: "__clk_is_enabled" [drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase.ko] undefined!

This is reached on x86_64, where x86_64_defconfig does not enable
CONFIG_COMMON_CLK (it is an ARM/SoC-centric option with no x86 consumer).
The same failure applies to any configuration that leaves it off.

Fix: compile the __clk_is_enabled() test only when CONFIG_COMMON_CLK is
available, and call clk_disable_unprepare() directly otherwise. Behaviour is
preserved exactly:

  - CONFIG_COMMON_CLK=y: unchanged, the enabled-clock test is performed.
  - CONFIG_COMMON_CLK=n: clk_disable_unprepare() is a no-op stub, and
    kbdev->clocks[] is never populated because clk_get() is a stub returning
    NULL, so the loop body is unreachable in practice.

Choosing this over setting CONFIG_COMMON_CLK=y in the profile fragment keeps
the kernel configuration at plain x86_64_defconfig, so no configuration delta
is introduced and the allowlist in research/program-scope.md section 5 is
untouched.

Validated against: Linux 6.12.111 (x86_64), r54p0-01eac0 with the six
patches/virtual-device patches applied. See analysis/findings.md F-17.

Applies after: patches/virtual-device/0001-0006.

--- a/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c
+++ b/product/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/mali_kbase_core_linux.c
@@ -3289,7 +3289,15 @@
 regulators_probe_defer:
 	for (i = 0; i < BASE_MAX_NR_CLOCKS_REGULATORS; i++) {
 		if (kbdev->clocks[i]) {
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_COMMON_CLK)
 			if (__clk_is_enabled(kbdev->clocks[i]))
+#else
+			/* clk_disable_unprepare() is a no-op stub here, and
+			 * kbdev->clocks[] is never populated without the common clock
+			 * framework, so this is equivalent. See analysis/findings.md F-17.
+			 */
+			if (1)
+#endif
 				clk_disable_unprepare(kbdev->clocks[i]);
 			clk_put(kbdev->clocks[i]);
 			kbdev->clocks[i] = NULL;
@@ -3326,7 +3334,12 @@
 
 	for (i = 0; i < BASE_MAX_NR_CLOCKS_REGULATORS; i++) {
 		if (kbdev->clocks[i]) {
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_COMMON_CLK)
 			if (__clk_is_enabled(kbdev->clocks[i]))
+#else
+			/* See the matching site in kbase_device_backend_init (F-17). */
+			if (1)
+#endif
 				clk_disable_unprepare(kbdev->clocks[i]);
 			clk_put(kbdev->clocks[i]);
 			kbdev->clocks[i] = NULL;
